---
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { executionStages, repositoryUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Documentation | Oxide Infer"
  description="Architecture, execution contracts, validation, and evidence for Oxide Infer."
  active="Docs"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation / Start</p>
    <h1>Start with the engine boundary.</h1>
    <p>
      Current source is an operator runtime. The accepted target is a
      standalone Oxide server and engine with an attributed, source-derived
      control plane and offline TileLang kernel artifacts.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Start" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Read in this order</h2>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <div class="doc-card">
          <span>01 / TARGET</span><h3>Engine architecture</h3>
          <p>Review Oxide server, engine, runtime, TileLang, and source ownership.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/design/standalone-oxide-engine.md`}>Open target architecture →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <span>02 / CURRENT</span><h3>Operator architecture</h3>
          <p>Inspect the transitional source that the engine plan will replace.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/design/oxide-infer-architecture.md`}>Open current architecture →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <span>03 / BENCHMARK</span><h3>Engine evidence</h3>
          <p>Compare kernels with FlashInfer and serving with vLLM and SGLang.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/development/engine-benchmark-plan.md`}>Open benchmark plan →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <span>04 / SURFACE</span><h3>Operator catalog</h3>
          <p>Check admitted dtypes, layouts, algorithms, and open gates.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/operator-catalog.md`}>Open catalog →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <span>05 / PROOF</span><h3>Evidence index</h3>
          <p>Inspect source revisions, methods, raw samples, and exclusions.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/README.md`}>Open evidence →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <span>06 / DEVICE</span><h3>Device validation</h3>
          <p>Run correctness, sanitizer, Graph, and performance gates separately. The current recorded target is H20.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/development/h20-validation.md`}>Open validation guide →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Execution lifecycle</h2>
      <p>Every admitted operator uses the same checked chain.</p>
      <ol class="lifecycle-list">
        {executionStages.map((stage) => (
          <li><span>{stage.key}</span><div><strong>{stage.name}</strong><p>{stage.detail}</p></div></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <pre><code>{`let plan = provider.plan(spec)?
let mut bindings = queue.bindings(capacity)?

let mut scope = queue.begin(bindings)?
plan.enqueue_into(&mut scope, operands)?
bindings = scope.finish().wait()?`}</code></pre>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Graph capture uses the same immutable plan.</strong>
        <p>Fixed-address Graph execution retains providers, bindings, functions, and completion resources.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Validate a checkout</h2>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/feichai0017/oxide-infer.git
cd oxide-infer
make check

# On the pinned CUDA host
make cuda-doctor
make cuda-check
make h20</code></pre>
      <p>
        A record applies only to its declared source, hardware, contract, and
        method. Device correctness does not imply performance, engine, or
        serving results.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
